{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1140398-vampires-entropy","id":1140398,"title":"Vampires: entropy?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-14T19:31:48-07:00","id":1140398,"title":"Vampires: entropy?","content":"Hi folks! So, I had a discussion with on of my friends lately about how M20 handles vampires. I'm okay with the books stating you'd have to have life and matter to affect them, because in my eyes vampires are exactly that, beings between living and death matter. Vitae is life, albeit a twisted form of it, in the end. However, he said that it should be matter and entropy, because vampires have nothing to do with life, they're dead, so entropy and that they're living only, because they're constantly accumulating entropic debt, which is manifesting through their weaknesses.<br /> <br /> What do you think on the matter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T23:41:03-07:00","id":1140436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1140398-vampires-entropy#post1140398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, he said that it should be matter and entropy, because vampires have nothing to do with life, they're dead, so entropy and that they're living only, because they're constantly accumulating entropic debt, which is manifesting through their weaknesses.<br /> <br /> What do you think on the matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>It really comes down to a kind of philosophy - are Vampires really dead, or is it Life trapped in a dead body, held in the process of dieing by absolute stasis and removal of Entropy? It's the latter that makes the 'Life and Matter' part work, as essentially they are seen as trapped right between those two states.<br /> <br /> Even if you go for the 'Life + Matter' route, Entropy can do BAD THINGS to Vampires. It's not like Life + Matter becomes the only way to harm them without resorting to fire. Kickstarting their entropy out of stasis will make their bodies behave like dead bodies should behave...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 09-15-2017, 07:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T06:26:56-07:00","id":1140504,"title":"","content":"You don't need the Life/Matter combo unless you are manipulating their pattern in a way that would require the Life sphere. Then Matter is needed as well, as they are essentially &quot;living matter&quot;.<br /> <br /> Any other effect, Entropy for example would not require the combo, it would work as it always does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T14:11:25-07:00","id":1140635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1140398-vampires-entropy?p=1140436#post1140436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It really comes down to a kind of philosophy - are Vampires really dead, or is it Life trapped in a dead body, held in the process of dieing by absolute stasis and removal of Entropy? It's the latter that makes the 'Life and Matter' part work, as essentially they are seen as trapped right between those two states.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, we settled for, after a while that we're seeing the state of vampires and entropy quite differently, hence the differences. He has a firm Catholic upbringing and I'm a... Gunno, agnostic materialist, maybe? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So our personal worldviews clearly colored our stances.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even if you go for the 'Life + Matter' route, Entropy can do BAD THINGS to Vampires. It's not like Life + Matter becomes the only way to harm them without resorting to fire. Kickstarting their entropy out of stasis will make their bodies behave like dead bodies should behave... </div> </div> </div>Oh, absolutely!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}